A Pyroam exact-`Fraction` evaluation using Machin bounds for `pi` and integer-square-root bounds for `sqrt(Delta_2)` reproduced:

```text
T=1.880: P5/D > .35392526, N5/D > .88481316, Branch-R I5/D > 1.02283423
T=1.900: P5/D > .30392526, N5/D > .75981316, Branch-R I5/D > .77283423
T=1.920: P5/D > .25392526, N5/D > .63481316, Branch-R I5/D > .52283423
T=1.950: P5/D > .17892526, N5/D > .44731316, Branch-R I5/D > .14783423
T=1.960: P5/D > .15392526, N5/D > .38481316, Branch-R I5/D > .02283423
T=2.000: P5/D > .05392526, N5/D > .13481316
T=2.020: P5/D > .00392526, N5/D > .00981316.
```

The candidate rounds downward throughout.

**Verdict:** PASS.

## 8. What this does not prove

The widened pentagon sea is structural, not an exclusion.  At `t=2.02` the forced population is small, and Branch R ceases to force rhombus/pentagon incidences before the pentagon floor itself vanishes.  The O--O hub path still has its own separately certified endpoint and is not extended by this argument.

The gain is scope: a large part of the previously unstructured high-`t` full-core regime now carries explicit source-empty pentagonal defects, and Branch R carries an explicit rhombic-pentagon interface through `t<=1.96`.

**Final verdict:** **PASS.** The scope propagation and all displayed endpoint constants are valid. C-II remains open.
